# Copy to .env and fill in real values. Never commit .env.
#
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LOCAL mode (hermetic, no credentials required)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Everything in this section has safe defaults. With no keys at all the system
# still runs end to end:
#   - the Diagnosis Agent uses the explicitly-marked deterministic TEST
#     fallback (AEGISOPS_LLM_FALLBACK=test) - never presented as model output
#   - ArmorIQ governed mode does not activate; incidents run UNGUARDED and the
#     intent-token step reports intent_token_status="not_configured" honestly
# Run:  scripts/run_incident.sh
#
# Per-agent identities (Phase 5). One ArmorIQ API key + per-request email
# scopes. The values below are the PLAN §5 defaults; override per deployment.
# They are identity/scope labels only - NOT ArmorIQ credentials.
# AEGISOPS_COMMANDER_EMAIL=commander@aegisops.local
# AEGISOPS_LOG_AGENT_EMAIL=log_agent@aegisops.local
# AEGISOPS_DIAGNOSIS_AGENT_EMAIL=diagnosis_agent@aegisops.local
# AEGISOPS_REMEDIATION_AGENT_EMAIL=remediation_agent@aegisops.local
#
# Delegation + audit (Phase 6/7). Delegated-token validity in seconds (shorter
# than the root token, per SDK design); audit mirror DB location (gitignored).
# AEGISOPS_DELEGATION_VALIDITY=300
# AEGISOPS_AUDIT_DB=database/audit.db
#
# Agent/MCP transport - defaults shown; override only when deploying agents on
# different hosts. The MCP URLs are what local MCP servers bind
# (127.0.0.1:8081-8083). For LIVE ArmorIQ enforcement the MCPs must additionally
# be registered on the ArmorIQ platform with public HTTPS URLs (see LIVE below).
# AEGISOPS_LOG_AGENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8091
# AEGISOPS_DIAGNOSIS_AGENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8092
# AEGISOPS_REMEDIATION_AGENT_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8093
# AEGISOPS_COMMANDER_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8094
# AEGISOPS_LOG_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8081/mcp
# AEGISOPS_DIAGNOSTIC_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8082/mcp
# AEGISOPS_REMEDIATION_MCP_URL=http://127.0.0.1:8083/mcp

# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# LIVE mode (real ArmorIQ enforcement + real Gemini diagnosis)
# ---------------------------------------------------------------------------
# Required. Must start with ak_live_, ak_test_, or ak_claw_.
# Get it from the ArmorIQ dashboard (platform.armoriq.ai -> API Keys)
# or run `armoriq login` (writes ~/.armoriq/credentials.json instead).
# Replace with your real key; the value below is a non-functional placeholder.
# ARMORIQ_API_KEY=ak_test_replace_with_your_real_key
#
# Optional - pick an environment
# ARMORIQ_ENV=production
#
# Optional - endpoint overrides (only needed for self-hosting / local dev)
# IAP_ENDPOINT=https://iap.armoriq.ai
# PROXY_ENDPOINT=https://proxy.armoriq.ai
# BACKEND_ENDPOINT=https://api.armoriq.ai
# USE_PRODUCTION=true
#
# Diagnosis LLM (Phase 4/5) - Google Gemini, official google-genai SDK.
# Model verified against the official Gemini API docs (ai.google.dev,
# 2026-08-20): gemini-3.5-flash-lite is the current stable (GA) Flash-Lite
# model (released 2026-07-21; gemini-3.1-flash-lite is deprecated in its
# favour). Key from https://aistudio.google.com/app/apikey
# Required for real model diagnoses. With no key, the Diagnosis Agent fails
# clearly, or uses the explicitly-marked deterministic TEST fallback when
# AEGISOPS_LLM_FALLBACK=test is set (never presented as a real model result).
# Replace with your real key; the value below is a non-functional placeholder.
# AEGISOPS_GEMINI_API_KEY=replace_with_your_gemini_api_key
# AEGISOPS_LLM_MODEL=gemini-3.5-flash-lite
# AEGISOPS_LLM_TIMEOUT=30
# AEGISOPS_LLM_FALLBACK=test
#
# LIVE ENFORCEMENT NOTE (Phase 8/9):
# To exercise governed enforcement end to end, the three MCP servers must be
# REGISTERED on the ArmorIQ platform (log-mcp, diagnostic-mcp, remediation-mcp)
# with public HTTPS URLs the ArmorIQ proxy can reach (e.g. a tunnel to
# 127.0.0.1:8081-8083). The local AEGISOPS_*_MCP_URL values above stay the
# agents' own local addresses; ArmorIQ invoke() routes through its proxy.
# scripts/preflight.py reports live readiness honestly - it never assumes it.